  "scope": "# 576426a573af \u2014 v2.2.0 \u2014 review-314653c4a38c2ca6\n\nDefect: first-conflict-only rivals fitted every baseline sample; invalid seed/index scalars were accepted.\nRepair: redundant 2..4-conflict witnesses, strict scalars, connected placement, and 12.5% recolored TRAIN-geometry anchors.\nFinal generator SHA-256: `d49ae2e612265752d5ce3cec5982071c6c6d96bb35183a47dff37719fd2eb0be`.\nChecks: full strict battery 12/12 green; portable tests 266/266 pass; exact source patch replayed and fresh tests 266/266 pass.\nLessons: four demos + one query; 300/300 production lessons and all 1,500 leave-one-out rotations pass three named rivals (1,491 distinct inputs).\nSchedule: all eight starts, seed 0, three bands; 24/24 lessons and 120/120 rotations pass (32 distinct inputs).\nFour-query production: four demos + four distinct queries, eight distinct inputs, eight Racket labels, 4/4 queries identified from demos.\nPrototype: proposed axis/precedence extension; four settings each retain two demos + four distinct queries; 16/16 setting/query checks pass.\nAuthority: original Racket rule unchanged (`892d64eecd2e`); no approval changes; no remaining blocker; finite support and withheld solve correctness remain explicit.\nAcceptance: routine for the canonical repair; parameter variants remain proposed.\n\n## What is included",
